     fhir:div [ fhir:v "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: TestPlan eu-api-document-publisher-tests</b></p><a name=\"eu-api-document-publisher-tests\"> </a><a name=\"hceu-api-document-publisher-tests\"> </a><p><b>Scopes</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Reference</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr><td><code>http://hl7.eu/fhir/health-data-api/ActorDefinition/document-publisher-actor-eu-api</code></td><td>The Document Publisher, a client that obtains a SMART Backend Services token, looks the patient up and publishes documents by Simplified Publish [ITI-105], is the system under test. The test bed plays the Access Provider.</td></tr></table><p><b>1 Suite: SMART Backend Services authorization</b></p><p>Rule: SMART Backend Services authorization — the scenarios grouped under it in the feature file.</p><p><b>Inputs</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>File</b></td></tr><tr><td>gherkin-script</td><td>eu-api-document-publisher.feature</td></tr></table><p><b>Tests</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Operation</b></td></tr><tr><td>pub-001 The SUT authenticates with a signed JWT client assertion (RFC 7523)</td><td>Fixture contract: fixtures/provider-v1/manifest.json, cases.pub-001 (input bindings and expected data). Covers security.smart-backend-services.</td><td>gherkin/Scenario</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>2 Suite: Patient lookup [ITI-78]</b></p><p>Rule: Patient lookup [ITI-78] — the scenarios grouped under it in the feature file.</p><p><b>Inputs</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>File</b></td></tr><tr><td>gherkin-script</td><td>eu-api-document-publisher.feature</td></tr></table><p><b>Tests</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Operation</b></td></tr><tr><td>pub-002 The SUT looks the patient up by identifier with a bearer token</td><td>Fixture contract: fixtures/provider-v1/manifest.json, cases.pub-002 (input bindings and expected data). Covers Patient.search-type, Patient.search.identifier.</td><td>gherkin/Scenario</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>3 Suite: Simplified Publish [ITI-105]</b></p><p>Rule: Simplified Publish [ITI-105] — the scenarios grouped under it in the feature file.</p><p><b>Inputs</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>File</b></td></tr><tr><td>gherkin-script</td><td>eu-api-document-publisher.feature</td></tr></table><p><b>Tests</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Operation</b></td></tr><tr><td>pub-003 The SUT creates a DocumentReference with the document embedded</td><td>Fixture contract: fixtures/provider-v1/manifest.json, cases.pub-003 (input bindings and expected data). Covers DocumentReference.create.</td><td>gherkin/Scenario</td></tr><tr><td>pub-004 The SUT publishes only the minimal metadata profile it claims</td><td>Fixture contract: fixtures/provider-v1/manifest.json, cases.pub-004 (input bindings and expected data). Covers DocumentReference.create.</td><td>gherkin/Scenario</td></tr><tr><td>pub-005 After a 401 the SUT obtains a fresh token before retrying</td><td>Fixture contract: fixtures/provider-v1/manifest.json, cases.pub-005 (input bindings and expected data). Covers security.authorization.</td><td>gherkin/Scenario</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>4 Suite: Transport security</b></p><p>Rule: Transport security — the scenarios grouped under it in the feature file.</p><p><b>Inputs</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>File</b></td></tr><tr><td>gherkin-script</td><td>eu-api-document-publisher.feature</td></tr></table><p><b>Tests</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Operation</b></td></tr><tr><td>pub-006 TLS 1.2 or higher is used for all communications</td><td>Fixture contract: fixtures/provider-v1/manifest.json, cases.pub-006 (input bindings and expected data